{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia","id":1377937,"title":"So what is Vampire going to do with Asia?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-02T06:08:51-07:00","id":1377937,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> So what is Vampire going to do with Asia?","content":"People say Whitewolf is canning Kueijin. I mean I don't want them retconned, if they did they would need to rewrite the whole regions history.<br /> <br /> But one possibility I see them doing is have the Wan Gui go through similar Changes as the Cainites, ultimately ending up making their character Creation closer to that of the Kindred, even to the point of having their Disciplines kind of merge with the Cainite Discipline options.<br /> <br /> Me personally I just want them to revise the Wan Gui, have the Kueijin be just a joke name forgotten or maybe something Western Vampires use when not using Cathayan. They just need a revision on par with what Changeling 20 got. I would be so happy to get Wan Gui with functional Rules and a book that condenses their gameline into 500 pages. :P<br /> <br /> What are you doing with Wan Gui Territory?<br /> <br /> I'm assuming most are either just ignoring the area because we don't have a revision, or they just replace them with normal Cainite Clans. Or... they just use the old rules and wing it when things don't work.<br /> <br /> The problem with saying the Normal Clans always stomped around in China and Japan is it removes the cool backstory of the Ravnos and Zapathsura vs the 10,000 Demons, and two it really feels like one of the Major Clans would have had China as their Homeland, I mean I was always found of Zao-lot being Asian rather then bald and white as portrayed in some kindred statues depicting him.<br /> <br /> Thoughts, hopes, dreams, suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T10:00:19-07:00","id":1377976,"title":"","content":"Setting aside 'The Kuei-Jin Question' which a lot of good digital ink has already been spilled over and some of my contemporary thoughts are along with the most recent of those threads, but that aside, I'll just suffice to say that I think the Kuei-Jin are fine but problematic when they replace White Wolf's traditional vampiric slot with themselves.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think Asia would be best handed by having its own vampiric sect(s) appropriate to local cultures and leadership styles alongside an existing population of Kuei-Jin and vampiric style bygones (but the latter is more the domain of discussion for other gamelines).<br /> <br /> In my own headcanon and home games I've always considered Asian Vampires to fall under an umbrella term of 'Black Courts' which represent a federation formed from a variety of pre-existing dynasties, courts, and organizations which drew together under a common banner in response to the existential threat of Camarilla, Sabbat, and the Anarch Movement during European exploration, colonization, and imperialism.<br /> <br /> Throughout most of its vampiric history, I'd say it's likely that Asia witnessed a situation similar to dark ages Europe (Courts of Love, Baronies of Avalon, Voivodate, etc) with significant regional powers eventually forming as a reflection of mortal geo-politics but following a mideveal paradigm of tradition and law until they were forced to modernize somewhat with the creation of the Black Courts (or whatever you wanna call it, I have a friend who uses 'Scarlet Court' instead).<br /> <br /> Regarding clans, I'd keep the primary 13 and scatter them as geographically appropriate as well as exercise the right to create bloodlines in order to provide for specific and regional vampiric lore to be represented; in the great White Wolf fashion of having nearly every splat represent most everything in some form or another.<br /> <br /> I'm also perfectly happy to explore alternative folklore, philosophies, mythologies, and theologies for the vampires of the continent and their purpose and origins. I've always been a fan of creating a vagueness about the past and vampiric origins and this is a prime time for it. I don't know enough about the vast spectrum of Asian religions and philosophies to propose one at this moment but I'm sure that, to an interested body, there's plenty of inspiration to draw upon for a story to be made.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, that's how I take it. We have vampires (in the Cainite since) everywhere else, the exclusion of Asia is glaring and should be rectified. I'm happy to have them co-exist alongside Kuei-Jin, Drowned Legacies, Bygones, or any other vampiric representative for those uncomfortable with the Cainite Abrahamic Tradition, but for me personally, having kindred having always had a presence in Asia is a retcon/headcanon that makes sense and would be supremally useful for writers, storytellers, and players alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T10:13:10-07:00","id":1377979,"title":"","content":"To be honest, as a native chinese I just want WW to revise, not retcon KotE. I hope they can simply ignore all stupid racism things, stereotypes and broken languages and all those out of date, repair the flawed system and make a more international, modern KotE. The general structure and theme are good and interesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-02-2020, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T10:31:02-07:00","id":1377988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1377979#post1377979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, as a native chinese I just want WW to revise, not retcon KotE. I hope they can simply ignore all stupid racism things, stereotypes and broken languages and all those out of date, repair the flawed system and make a more international, modern KotE. The general structure and theme is good and interesting</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope so too. But then again they kept the Hsien over in Changeling and they didn't use the Pinyin Xian. The Name Kueijin is silly but the book title Kindred of the East is solid, even though they go on to explain they aren't Kindred.<br /> <br /> I hope they just Fix them, but I want them to at least decide so people can prepare and do work on it themselves. and have it be somewhere of the ballpark of how the line is going.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T10:46:59-07:00","id":1377994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1377988#post1377988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope so too. But then again they kept the Hsien over in Changeling and they didn't use the Pinyin Xian. The Name Kueijin is silly but the book title Kindred of the East is solid, even though they go on to explain they aren't Kindred.<br /> <br /> I hope they just Fix them, but I want them to at least decide so people can prepare and do work on it themselves. and have it be somewhere of the ballpark of how the line is going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all of them are stubborn, Gods &amp; Monsters of M20 uses \u201cJiangshi\u201d and \u201cQi\u201d, and they are obviously KotE. Book of Fallen and Meixiu section use Diyu, not Yomi. But as you say, they should work on themselves first and then the culture things mostly I think<br /> <br /> But to be honest it is difficult to make them really do something about the line. KotE is always a minor gameline and can\u2019t make much money<br /> <br /> And, the whole KotE is, a typical 90\u2019s western oriental work, which is filled with the all prejudices and stereotypes of westerners in that era. The anime, Hong Kong elements, Orienal Mystism and full of Kung Fu. Everything is stupid and ridiculous today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-02-2020, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T10:55:36-07:00","id":1377997,"title":"","content":"Yeah that is the issue with Niche products, I am a fan of them but if they need to work on them to make them work or they need to replace them they will be placed on the backburner because they are niche. And because of that Asia seems to be in a limbo state, meanwhile at least the Laibon are functional with the current system, their wonkiest system translation is their unique form of Morality that uses a duel score representing a humanity/worldly stat and a supernatural/otherworldly stat.<br /> <br /> Oh nice I didn't read my copy of Book of the Fallen all the way through yet. Yeah its wonky to have Chi somewhere and then Qi somewhere else, and then toss in Ki every now and then. Though its nice flavor for old school Wan Gui to have mention of Prana to tie that old Sanskrit feel.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I just want the region to not be locked in limbo so it can be developed one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T11:17:43-07:00","id":1378002,"title":"","content":"Retconning the Kuei-Jin is a terrible idea. Their unique and don't need to be changed that much- maybe some of the excess stuff regarding them streamlined. The reason why I say this because it wouldn't make sense to have Kindred in Asia if we consider the history of oWoD. I've already dug in the conflicts of this lore mishmash before in other posts, the August Personage of Jade vs the Abrahamic God thing really clash with eachother. Caine and none of his childer beside Saulot were active in East Asia at all. There are no established vampire clans in Asia. Not having Vampires in Asia is not really exclusion at all, it makes sense they aren't there from a logical and lore perspective. Retconning Kuei-Jin would desecrate all the loving work that was put in KotE and have it stand on its own two feet instead of shoving Kindred everywhere where it doesn't make sense. Asia isn't in a limbo state, there is clear material on it already. Just remove all the racial tagging/stereotypes from KotE and call it a day.<br /> <br /> Also I disagree what you say about the Laibon. Africa should've gotten its own unique splat like Asia did. The Laibon are horrible tbh because lorewise it doesn't make sense. How can Caine from the middle-east and his subsequent childe supersede African populations where Vampirism started in the middle-east and went downstream to Africa from Antediluvians visiting it there? If we take actual biological history in account (since WTA confirms the oWoD universe went through how our earth evolved and the inclusion of dinosaurs basically) the first murderer would've been some random African tribal. Even discounting that little snippet, Laibon should've never been made. They like I said before should've thought of a new splat for Africa or just left it alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-02-2020, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T11:37:21-07:00","id":1378007,"title":"","content":"I would prefer the Kindred of the East stays as well. But they are in a limbo state concerning new products because they don't know how they will move forward with new products.<br /> <br /> I disagree on the Laibon issue. Nothing says the first Murder didn't happen in Africa. And we don't know where the First City was exactly and even if it was in the Middle East Caine could have wander there from Ethiopia or anywhere else.<br /> <br /> Laibon were an attempt at making a new splat but one a little more closely tied then Kindred of the East. August Personage of Jade could be the same as the Abrahamic Gods as far as Vampires of all types are concerned. After all their is implication The Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Empress are Angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T11:57:52-07:00","id":1378013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378002#post1378002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Laibon are horrible tbh because lorewise it doesn't make sense. How can Caine from the middle-east and his subsequent childe supersede African populations where Vampirism started in the middle-east and went downstream to Africa from Antediluvians visiting it there?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, from at least the Revised Clanbooks onward the writers seem to have been toning down the &quot;Caine is canon&quot; thing (which I very much approve of). The Setites have their own creation myth that has nothing to do with the God of Abraham, and they say their oldest elders can remember when the whole Caine story was first invented and popularized. The Lasombra clanbook has a whole section picking apart the Caine mythology and pointing out the flaws in it. The BH/Assamites agree with most of the stories of the Antediluvians but disagree with the genealogy from the Book of Nod, and have their own version of it.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the Clanbook Lasombra Revised take. The Antediluvians existed, sure, but any stories about what came before them should be taken with many grains of salt. Suppose, hypothetically, that some massive apocalypse happened nowadays and only a few dozen eighth-gens survived, with no written records of what came before; how long do you think they'd keep calling themselves &quot;eighth&quot; instead of something more impressive? How long do you think it would take before the descendants of those eighth-gens came up with a new mythology about them, rewriting the details to make a better story? Probably less than four millennia, right?<br /> <br /> And once that all happened\u2026doesn't it seem entirely plausible that the descendants of a separate, unrelated eighth-gen (or group of them) might turn out to have survived in a different part of the world, with a different mythos around them, that doesn't fit at all into the new stories that have built up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T14:14:52-07:00","id":1378043,"title":"","content":"\u2022This is me asking because I'm genuinely curious, where do the terms 'Pinyin Xian' mean? If it's something that I could use as a more accurate term for Hsien, like 'Jiangshi' for Kuei-Jin I'd definitely be interested in adding it to my repertoire.<br /> <br /> \u2022As far as ret-conning the Kuei-Jin I can see how they work being usable but I agree that correcting terms and grounding the culture and themes more accurately would be useful for both the game and western-eastern cultural contact generally. I've said before, I don't mind the Kuei-Jin existing in some form, I simply think it does the most good to have them co-exist alongside VtM vampires (which I'll be calling 'kindred' going forward).<br /> <br /> \u2022I can see how one can argue that the Abrahamic G-D and the August Personage of Jade being unified could be problematic however using the WoD lense of them being faces/aspects/names for The One Above as a perfect cosmic Everything, I think it works.<br /> <br /> \u2022Justifying having no Asian kindred because there aren't many Asian kindred is a bit of a circular argument imo. Even then though, by advised, it wasn't exactly true. [Ravnos], Cappadocian and The Eldest are described as having wandered east, same as Saulot. There's no reason one can't say that other clans didn't wander as well. Ennoia was known to wander everywhere, with Gangrel showing up from Scandinavia to Sub-Saharan Africa to Mongolia to North America. Central and South America had a settite bloodline! Vampires are defined as being parasites and dark reflections of humanity, it makes no sense to me for them not to exist everywhere that humans exist in enough numbers to support them and Asia, as the largest populated continent on Earth, seems glaring by ommision.<br /> <br /> \u2022I'm not saying that Kindred of the East doesn't have a certain amount of heart and that care wasn't taken in its creation, but seeking to improve the World of Darkness isn't desecrating prior editions. It's seeking to work together and create something amazing for everyone to be able to enjoy.<br /> <br /> \u2022[Moving a quick reply to Draconis here because I think the Laibon reply has more oomph as a finishing point], I'm perfectly happy with obfuscating whether or not the Caine story is true, even though I'm fond of it. Cain doesn't arise in Jewish tradition until sometime in the third-fourth millennia BCE to the best of my knowledge, so I think it's perfectly valid that the first vampire wasn't originally called Cain and The One Above might not have originally been called the Abraham G-D. However, I do think this is interesting: even though they weren't originally those things, they've taken on those contexts so we can understand them. The One is too massive to comprehend and pre-Gaubtlet reality is nigh on impossible to understand. So just because the action of the first murder which created vampires didn't happen, doesn't mean it was done by Cain. On the other hand though, if everyone thinks it was Cain, that 'Cain' is the name of that legendary pre-historical figure, it might as well be Cain.<br /> <br /> \u2022Laibon are similarly controversial to the Kuei-Jim but less commonly discussed. I'm personally for having them be the template for what the Kuei-Jin could be. A unique and distinct vampiric group that is culturally grounded in a region and co-exists along with kindred. That aside, the specific timeline of World of Darkness is muddy, due to Consensus and the Multi-Resonance Layered Reality. So, for discussing humanity in the WoD, you get to have fun with this: Cain was the fifth (counting Lilith &amp; The Second Woman) human being, Cain is a figure from Jewish theology, humanity most likely arose from parts of Ethiopia and almost certainly originated in Africa. All of these statements are simultaneously true in WoD. Therefore, as the fifth human in the abrahamic sense, Cain has plenty of opportunity to spread his curse to all his brother's descendants, before and after The Flood. However, even taking the Biblical Context aside, vampirism would still reach throughout Africa and Asia. Why? Because humans did. Humanity has been traveling for millennia. Chinese ambassadors reached Rome and Ethiopian coins have been found in India. Kindred vampirism is a parasitic reflection and it follows humanity and it festers everywhere where human blood is prevalent enough to support it. By its own logic, functions, and prerogative; the kindred curse should have passed to every populated corner of the world, even if some took centuries or millennia to reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T14:40:39-07:00","id":1378050,"title":"","content":"Its not a glaring omission at all. The Kuei-Jin wouldn't allow Cainites to encroach on Asia at all really. The only foothold they ever had was in India. Also the &quot;Multi-Resonance Layered Reality&quot; thing is again from D:TF (Demon: The Fallen) which like I've said numerous times before basically affirms the Abrahamic viewpoint of VTM entirely which retroactively retcons alot of other splats. The August Personage of Jade and Abrahamic God are clearly different entities entirely. There were no Vampires in Asia (East Asia atleast) at all, there were just the Wan Xian before they got corrupted by the Yama Kings. In their uncorrupted state where they focused on fighting monsters- of course they wouldn't have been any Vampires in Asia, even thereafter when they became Kuei-Jin their would be a double reason to keep out Vampires from Asia- competition for mortals.<br /> <br /> Taking that all into account anyways, it just doesn't make sense for Vampires to have holdings or any significant presence in the most of Asia- at best maybe they make a push in modern times for some territory there- a reverse Great Leap Forward the Kuei-Jin commenced (and are still doing if the V5 writers hopefully don't forget about or scrap it). Besides there already has been a vampiric bloodline in Asia, the Anda I think. They didn't last very long because the Kuei-Jin took them out IIRC. Suddenly adding in random Bloodlines into Asia out of nowhere make sense, like a whole brood of Vampires just pop-up out of nowhere in the middle of Asia in the middle of deep Kuei-jin territory. Even if there was to be some Vampire bloodlines added into Asia, there'd not have much of a presence because they'd also be on the down low hiding from the Kuei-Jin presumably. V5 writers don't really like bloodlines anywhere with how we've seen them handle making the whole &quot;Hecata&quot; Clan nonsense anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-02-2020, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T14:44:53-07:00","id":1378051,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d really like to see V5 do something with Asia, but I\u2019m only a little familiar with the Wan Kuei. I\u2019ll probably just go along with what everyone else wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T16:05:53-07:00","id":1378070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378043#post1378043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is me asking because I'm genuinely curious, where do the terms 'Pinyin Xian' mean? If it's something that I could use as a more accurate term for Hsien, like 'Jiangshi' for Kuei-Jin I'd definitely be interested in adding it to my repertoire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pinyin is a newer romanization system for Mandarin, and the most official one at this point. &quot;Hsien&quot; and &quot;Xian&quot; represent the same word, but &quot;Hsien&quot; is in Wade-Giles romanization (the most popular system for most of the 20th century) and &quot;Xian&quot; is in modern pinyin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T16:20:28-07:00","id":1378075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378043#post1378043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm perfectly happy with obfuscating whether or not the Caine story is true, even though I'm fond of it. Cain doesn't arise in Jewish tradition until sometime in the third-fourth millennia BCE to the best of my knowledge, so I think it's perfectly valid that the first vampire wasn't originally called Cain and The One Above might not have originally been called the Abraham G-D. However, I do think this is interesting: even though they weren't originally those things, they've taken on those contexts so we can understand them. The One is too massive to comprehend and pre-Gaubtlet reality is nigh on impossible to understand. So just because the action of the first murder which created vampires didn't happen, doesn't mean it was done by Cain. On the other hand though, if everyone thinks it was Cain, that 'Cain' is the name of that legendary pre-historical figure, it might as well be Cain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I personally like anything more than a couple millennia back to be shrouded in mystery\u2014written records didn't exist at all, anywhere, before somewhere around 4000 BCE, and oral histories can change a lot over time. So I always introduce a lot of ambiguity and uncertainty around anything pre-Antediluvian. The thirteen clan founders definitely exist/existed, there's proof of that, but any stories prior to them have been passed down through generations upon generations upon generations, and even immortal memories aren't infallible (see, for example, the Sargon Fragment which contained secrets Cappadocius had recorded himself but had lost over the millennia).<br /> <br /> There's nothing whatsoever wrong with the Cain mythos existing and vampires believing it, or even with it being canon that vampires originated with the first act of murder. I just don't like the pre-Antediluvian myths being treated as 100% OOC canon, and all the other in-universe legends (like vampires originating with Lilith or with Set) being treated as canonically wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T16:33:31-07:00","id":1378082,"title":"","content":"Ah, gotcha Draconis, thank ya, good to know.<br /> <br /> \u2022If one likes the Kuei-Jin as written then sure, that justification works fine, heck, its built into the Kuei-Jin from the ground up. They kept kindred out of all of Asia, the Anda and Salubri were flukes, maybe a bit during European Imperialism but that's it. If you like as written, that's fair and fine. I'll be honest though, I still don't think it makes much practical sense. Kindred are like rats, once you have them there almost impossible to fully root out. Asia has an enormous population and ancient trade routes to Europe, India, the Near East, and Africa; giving plenty of opportunity for millennia. Plus, Kuei-Jin and Kindred, to the best of my recollection, feed on distinct parts of mortals and so there's not necessarily any need for instant and extreme antagonism between them, or at least, no more reason then what also exists with every other supernatural species. Plus, if we compare supernaturals, the separation seems even more flawed. Just about every other splat hates vampires on principle, yet vampires haven't gone anywhere for all the mages in France or werewolves in America or changelings in Ireland. It just seems like the separation is a Hand of God (as in the writers) forced division between Asia and The Rest, effectively creating two settings, which is a lot of people's biggest complaint about Kinsred of the East to begin with.<br /> <br /> \u2022You yourself included WtA in your argument, so I figured that pulling from other splats in my rebuttal was fair game. We've also already talked at length about our differing views regarding the concept of Multi-Resonance Layered Reality, so probably no need to get into it here.<br /> <br /> \u2022Even assuming that the Wan Xian and Kuei-Jin had the power to fully eradicate the presence of kindred and the willingness to do so, how do you justify in canon why the Wan Xian only ever tried to eradicate vampires outside East Asia, since there mandate would imply it spread to all the world? How do you have the Salubri and Saulot the Thief? The existence of the Anda bloodline, the Ravnos war with the Kuei-Jin in India, that kindred have made footholds in canon and that a prominent reason why the Mandinarate (or whatever it was called) was successfully established was that an already scattered and collapsing California Free State was collapsing and undergoing Midnight Siege from the Camarilla and Sabbat? Taking that all together, it doesn't make much sense to me, unless one gives Kuei-Jin power on scale with archmages and incarna.<br /> <br /> \u2022V5 aside, I also doubt much of this would get taken up by the writers, but this was a thread asking individuals their opinions and routes, so I brought up my own. I prefer a long standing kindred presence in Asia which co-exists alongside the Kuei-Jin with unique bloodlines and organizations, but a retcon of such proportions would probably require at least an entire book dedicated to it and given the eternal controversy of The Kuei-Jin Question, I doubt anything will ever come to that.<br /> <br /> At the end of the night, these are just my personal thoughts, opinions, and headcanons. Whatever you do, as long as you and your table are happy, is valid af.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T17:06:30-07:00","id":1378097,"title":"","content":"I'm going to fold the kue jin into the clans. Its a project on my long term to do list. Then I will just turn the different courts into their own sects and tada!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T17:27:03-07:00","id":1378102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378097#post1378097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to fold the kue jin into the clans. Its a project on my long term to do list. Then I will just turn the different courts into their own sects and tada!</div> </div> </div> </div>So it will be like you choose a Clan, then you choose a Dharma, kind of like Werewolf? Are you going to introduce new Clan Variants?<br /> <br /> It would be interesting because the Dharmas interact and form groups with each other, Forming Wu's if I recall their Coterie equivalent were. So its like a region that kept their Old Roads (The way vampires divided in the Dark Ages). Its interesting because if you make the different courts different sects its like a region with lots of potential rivals except people often stay in their own territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T17:54:15-07:00","id":1378120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378070#post1378070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pinyin is a newer romanization system for Mandarin, and the most official one at this point. &quot;Hsien&quot; and &quot;Xian&quot; represent the same word, but &quot;Hsien&quot; is in Wade-Giles romanization (the most popular system for most of the 20th century) and &quot;Xian&quot; is in modern pinyin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it more conducive to Mandarin the most widely spoken of the Chinese Dialects, and it comes at it more like it developed for native speakers to translate their words, while Wade Giles comes at it more from European languages trying to translate the sounds into romanization, if that makes sense. But seeing Wade Giles dates the books, it brings to mind when I read books written like in the 80s. Its good for some flavor, like it evokes the old Hong Kong writings before they stopped being British in 97.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378082#post1378082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, gotcha Draconis, thank ya, good to know.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378082#post1378082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u2022If one likes the Kuei-Jin as written then sure, that justification works fine, heck, its built into the Kuei-Jin from the ground up. They kept kindred out of all of Asia, the Anda and Salubri were flukes, maybe a bit during European Imperialism but that's it. If you like as written, that's fair and fine. I'll be honest though, I still don't think it makes much practical sense. Kindred are like rats, once you have them there almost impossible to fully root out. Asia has an enormous population and ancient trade routes to Europe, India, the Near East, and Africa; giving plenty of opportunity for millennia. Plus, Kuei-Jin and Kindred, to the best of my recollection, feed on distinct parts of mortals and so there's not necessarily any need for instant and extreme antagonism between them, or at least, no more reason then what also exists with every other supernatural species. Plus, if we compare supernaturals, the separation seems even more flawed. Just about every other splat hates vampires on principle, yet vampires haven't gone anywhere for all the mages in France or werewolves in America or changelings in Ireland. It just seems like the separation is a Hand of God (as in the writers) forced division between Asia and The Rest, effectively creating two settings, which is a lot of people's biggest complaint about Kinsred of the East to begin with.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u2022You yourself included WtA in your argument, so I figured that pulling from other splats in my rebuttal was fair game. We've also already talked at length about our differing views regarding the concept of Multi-Resonance Layered Reality, so probably no need to get into it here.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u2022Even assuming that the Wan Xian and Kuei-Jin had the power to fully eradicate the presence of kindred and the willingness to do so, how do you justify in canon why the Wan Xian only ever tried to eradicate vampires outside East Asia, since there mandate would imply it spread to all the world? How do you have the Salubri and Saulot the Thief? The existence of the Anda bloodline, the Ravnos war with the Kuei-Jin in India, that kindred have made footholds in canon and that a prominent reason why the Mandinarate (or whatever it was called) was successfully established was that an already scattered and collapsing California Free State was collapsing and undergoing Midnight Siege from the Camarilla and Sabbat? Taking that all together, it doesn't make much sense to me, unless one gives Kuei-Jin power on scale with archmages and incarna.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u2022V5 aside, I also doubt much of this would get taken up by the writers, but this was a thread asking individuals their opinions and routes, so I brought up my own. I prefer a long standing kindred presence in Asia which co-exists alongside the Kuei-Jin with unique bloodlines and organizations, but a retcon of such proportions would probably require at least an entire book dedicated to it and given the eternal controversy of The Kuei-Jin Question, I doubt anything will ever come to that.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">At the end of the night, these are just my personal thoughts, opinions, and headcanons. Whatever you do, as long as you and your table are happy, is valid af.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> See the big thing for me is it makes sense the Wan Gui curbed Kindred growth because they compete for the same resources. I would experiment though with Courts that share Kindred and Wan Gui, I could see something like that Forming in the Philippines with the strong Catholic presence along with old asian influences, or maybe Sri Lanka say its far enough away the Ravnos don't influence it with their war and old Kindred and Wan Gui form like a buddhist court or something.<br /> <br /> But it makes sense to me the Wan Gui would be prominent in Asia but the Cainites would have territory there as well. And possibly you could treat Cainites in Asia as being universally despised as untouchables in most courts, kind of like treating all Cainites as Caitiff in their eyes.<br /> <br /> But I don't personally believe the Cathayan Propaganda about Yah Boi Zao-lat. The hate and smears we hear come from the legacy of Zao-lots rival pupils to the Guru Xue. It really seems like a lot of it was bad press because they had sour grapes over a non Wan Gui learning the Dharmas, and after Xue Ascended we had no one but Zao-lots enemies recording history. Seriously I don't recall any proof for instance that Master Xue hated Zao-lat for some great crime.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But I just want them to address the region so that when somebody works on fleshing out the continent they don't later find out its contradictory to the direction the gameline goes in. Kind of like when they introduced the Bushi and Gaki and then backtracked and explain no no that was silly Cainites getting the Cathayans wrong.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T19:17:59-07:00","id":1378143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia#post1377937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People say Whitewolf is canning Kueijin. I mean I don't want them retconned, if they did they would need to rewrite the whole regions history.<br /> <br /> But one possibility I see them doing is have the Wan Gui go through similar Changes as the Cainites, ultimately ending up making their character Creation closer to that of the Kindred, even to the point of having their Disciplines kind of merge with the Cainite Discipline options.<br /> <br /> Me personally I just want them to revise the Wan Gui, have the Kueijin be just a joke name forgotten or maybe something Western Vampires use when not using Cathayan. They just need a revision on par with what Changeling 20 got. I would be so happy to get Wan Gui with functional Rules and a book that condenses their gameline into 500 pages. :P<br /> <br /> What are you doing with Wan Gui Territory?<br /> <br /> I'm assuming most are either just ignoring the area because we don't have a revision, or they just replace them with normal Cainite Clans. Or... they just use the old rules and wing it when things don't work.<br /> <br /> The problem with saying the Normal Clans always stomped around in China and Japan is it removes the cool backstory of the Ravnos and Zapathsura vs the 10,000 Demons, and two it really feels like one of the Major Clans would have had China as their Homeland, I mean I was always found of Zao-lot being Asian rather then bald and white as portrayed in some kindred statues depicting him.<br /> <br /> Thoughts, hopes, dreams, suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;No please God no&quot; &lt;- from The Office<br /> <br /> I REALLY like Kindred of the East as it is. Yes, it is complex, takes time to get used to, it's a different culture therefore a lot of research is needed, but once you get past that, it is a REALLY GREAT GAME.<br /> <br /> The line wasn't very popular back in the day but it did sold out San Francisco by Night fast enough that it needed to release that book as eBook soon after (IMHO, that book was the worst of the entire line). It had amazing characters like Liu Shao (WoD HK), Chiu Bao (NoP, DB-DT) and Lili Zhou (I let one of my PCs be the one to enact Taking the Left-Hand Path to her from Devil Tiger to Bone Flower). The August Body of Sagacious Devils was a great concept, and the settings of HK in transition from WoD 1st ed to what it became in WoDHK was probably one of the stories my players enjoyed the most.<br /> <br /> The entire line needed polishing, that's all. It missed many things like Nushi (only 3 examples in the whole line and none were explained in any Wu of By Night books) and the higher level disciplines weren't that good compared to how revised did them in Guide to the Camarilla/Sabbat/clanbooks. One thing that still bugs me is how the corebook is organized (it's a mess!), yesterday I needed to see some rules while STing and it took me a while to find exactly what I needed.<br /> <br /> I recall Saulot's image from Clanbook Tremere Revised (pg. 14) and Transylvania Chronicles IV (pg. 44) and none were bald, where else was he depicted? On Saulot being asian, it would explain the origin of Mokur (he was from the Jomon people, who are believed to be from 10000 BC up to 1000 BC during Japan's prehistory) and tying him to Japan island would make sense.<br /> <br /> - Saga<br /> <br /> PS: It's a really entertaining game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T19:24:57-07:00","id":1378145,"title":"","content":"I don't know how serious they were about ignoring Kindred of the East or just wanting to recycle it. I am not a fan of just redoing all this detailed setting, and they fit rather perfect with the other Middle Kingdom books.<br /> <br /> <br /> I forgot where I remember a description of a statue of Saulot and it was a bald European guy with a third eye. Where was it, was it Lair of the Hidden? No I don't think they had a statue of him there. I don't remember where I could have seen it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T19:46:07-07:00","id":1378156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378120#post1378120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yeah it more conducive to Mandarin the most widely spoken of the Chinese Dialects, and it comes at it more like it developed for native speakers to translate their words, while Wade Giles comes at it more from European languages trying to translate the sounds into romanization, if that makes sense. But seeing Wade Giles dates the books, it brings to mind when I read books written like in the 80s. Its good for some flavor, like it evokes the old Hong Kong writings before they stopped being British in 97.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I do have some problems when translating KotE<br /> <br /> It uses a mixture of all eastern asian languages, and some &quot;madarins&quot; I can't understand up to now. For instance, chi'n ta, the Lightning People, I can't find any suitable words in chinese dictionaries (even cantonese's !)</span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378143#post1378143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it is complex, takes time to get used to, it's a different culture therefore a lot of research is needed, but once you get past that, it is a REALLY GREAT GAME.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall dharma books, which may be less intersting when you look at first glance, for it discusses more about their own philosophy, and it may be boring at first. But when you clam down and read, you'll find many interesting ideas<br /> <br /> This also applies to the whole KotE, you will realize its shining points if you ignore those out of date (aka. racism, kungfukungfukungfu, etc.)<br /> <br /> I can see how serious WW is. They did do much research and released this line, although it's a bit flawed today<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378143#post1378143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The entire line needed polishing, that's all. It missed many things like Nushi (only 3 examples in the whole line and none were explained in any Wu of By Night books) and the higher level disciplines weren't that good compared to how revised did them in Guide to the Camarilla/Sabbat/clanbooks. One thing that still bugs me is how the corebook is organized (it's a mess!), yesterday I needed to see some rules while STing and it took me a while to find exactly what I needed.</span></span></div> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not only Nushi, advanced disciplines and some not that common ones (Kiai, Mibasham, etc.) never have examples, because there is not much room, maybe (aka. fewer supplements)<br /> <br /> And yeah, existed 6+ disciplines are quite flawed and need being repaired<br /> <br /> I also want to see more supplements, more advanced powers, Godbodies of Fourth Age, Bile Shintais, 6+ Rites and so on. All worth exploiting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-02-2020, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T19:53:25-07:00","id":1378160,"title":"","content":"Honestly the biggest fix is they need to Revamp the disciplines, with emphasis on the elder ones, and if we had that I could run them pretty well as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T20:01:49-07:00","id":1378161,"title":"","content":"I think Asia will mostly be ignored for a while at least. There are no simple and not deeply problematic ways to deal with the region and its people and culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T20:19:21-07:00","id":1378165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378161#post1378161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Asia will mostly be ignored for a while at least. There are no simple and not deeply problematic ways to deal with the region and its people and culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty simple don't treat the area like how all the 90's cartoons treated the Japan episode, tone down the Anime (which was mostly in the art style so no biggie) and do a bit of research and your good. Everything is tiptoeing and problematic now a days so that can only be avoided by ignoring it completely which is what they are doing. I don't want that.<br /> <br /> Kueijin isn't an offensive word, its just a silly one. And its appropriate for the Elder Wan Gui to be elitist racists China has a history of treating anything outside the Empires borders as backwards barbarians. And Japan emulated a lot of that with their class system. Over all the Wan Gui are going to have a lot of Confucian influences and China seems the dominant Culture. I would like a bit more Indian jockeying for that spot though. And Tibetan culture, Tengri beliefs, and animism of the many pacific nations should be sprinkled in. But it makes sense that the Quincunx and many Ancestors are elitist racists. How much they have to tone that down depends on how much they have to deal with cultures not their own. Indian Vampire Monks are probably not going to appreciate envoys from the Bushi and Quincunx insulting everyone else while they insult each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T20:38:17-07:00","id":1378169,"title":"","content":"Wan Kuei not Wan Gui.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T20:45:11-07:00","id":1378171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378169#post1378169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wan Kuei not Wan Gui.</div> </div> </div> </div>We were just over this Gui is the Pinyin form of Kuei which is wade Giles.<br /> <br /> This is the character \u9b3c its the character for ghost or demon. Its the same character for Mo Gui, which is what they called Gremlins in the movie Gremlins, which is just a word for evil spirit or demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T22:24:04-07:00","id":1378185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378156#post1378156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I do have some problems when translating KotE<br /> <br /> It uses a mixture of all eastern asian languages, and some &quot;madarins&quot; I can't understand up to now. For instance, chi'n ta, the Lightning People, I can't find any suitable words in chinese dictionaries (even cantonese's !)</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That may be something that they formed in Japanese (as shinta, which is listed right next to it) and back-read into some really mangled Wade-Giles Romanized Mandarin. Hazarding a guess, a simple </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u795e</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u4ed6, as Japanese sometimes uses </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u795e</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> for thunder. If that's an unsatisfying answer that doesn't work within the bounds of the languages in question... that's a depressing par for course, I'd say.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T22:25:27-07:00","id":1378187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378165#post1378165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's pretty simple don't treat the area like how all the 90's cartoons treated the Japan episode, tone down the Anime (which was mostly in the art style so no biggie) and do a bit of research and your good. Everything is tiptoeing and problematic now a days so that can only be avoided by ignoring it completely which is what they are doing. I don't want that.<br /> <br /> Kueijin isn't an offensive word, its just a silly one. And its appropriate for the Elder Wan Gui to be elitist racists China has a history of treating anything outside the Empires borders as backwards barbarians. And Japan emulated a lot of that with their class system. Over all the Wan Gui are going to have a lot of Confucian influences and China seems the dominant Culture. I would like a bit more Indian jockeying for that spot though. And Tibetan culture, Tengri beliefs, and animism of the many pacific nations should be sprinkled in. But it makes sense that the Quincunx and many Ancestors are elitist racists. How much they have to tone that down depends on how much they have to deal with cultures not their own. Indian Vampire Monks are probably not going to appreciate envoys from the Bushi and Quincunx insulting everyone else while they insult each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>By combining what's in Victorian Age Vampire and Clanbook Ravnos Revised, one can have a rough idea how is the Cainite society in India, I like that overview. V20 Dark Ages Companion contributed to that vibe when they wrote the Mogadishu chapter.<br /> <br /> When it comes to kueijin, we only have Kindred of the East Companion covering India or Bangladesh and some from Heresies of the Way (though I never was a fan of the heretical dharmas). Having Rangda and Ravana as antagonists and how they are portrayed was a great idea for the setting.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 04-03-2020, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T22:45:33-07:00","id":1378189,"title":"","content":"Best guess? They'll declare that whatever the kuejin version of gehenna was, happened.<br /> <br /> They'll also de-emphasize the kuejin by talking about all the cainites who survived by learning to avoid them, and even learned how to use them as a sort of shield to protect themselves from rival vampires.<br /> <br /> And now that the kuejin are extinct, all the cainites who were using them as de facto shields are scrambling to deal with both the good and bad results of this. On the good side, they have much more territory now. On the bad side, western cainites are now trickling in and trying to take over. The cainites of the east are really missing the kuejin, who were never all that numerous due to the excruciatingly slow method of their reproduction. The cainites of the east loved that these overrated, small in number, slow to reproduce, easy to avoid creatures inspired such terror from their western brethren. The kuejin were the boogeymen who protected the eastern cainites from western cainite invasion.<br /> <br /> Now that's over, and war is commencing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T23:00:17-07:00","id":1378190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378189#post1378189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Best guess? They'll declare that whatever the kuejin version of gehenna was, happened.<br /> <br /> They'll also de-emphasize the kuejin by talking about all the cainites who survived by learning to avoid them, and even learned how to use them as a sort of shield to protect themselves from rival vampires.<br /> <br /> And now that the kuejin are extinct, all the cainites who were using them as de facto shields are scrambling to deal with both the good and bad results of this. On the good side, they have much more territory now. On the bad side, western cainites are now trickling in and trying to take over. The cainites of the east are really missing the kuejin, who were never all that numerous due to the excruciatingly slow method of their reproduction. The cainites of the east loved that these overrated, small in number, slow to reproduce, easy to avoid creatures inspired such terror from their western brethren. The kuejin were the boogeymen who protected the eastern cainites from western cainite invasion.<br /> <br /> Now that's over, and war is commencing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy crap you might be right, they might have an Apocalypse genocide the Wan Gui host! I wonder how they would do it without it being a worldwide apocalypse, maybe the Yama Kings will have one of their number become the Demon Emperor and reclaim the escaped souls.<br /> <br /> It would be a shame but they seem like they want to just Tabula Rasa the region. And I think this would be the most expedient way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> They were such a fun concept too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T23:00:28-07:00","id":1378191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378189#post1378189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Best guess? They'll declare that whatever the kuejin version of gehenna was, happened.<br /> <br /> They'll also de-emphasize the kuejin by talking about all the cainites who survived by learning to avoid them, and even learned how to use them as a sort of shield to protect themselves from rival vampires.<br /> <br /> And now that the kuejin are extinct, all the cainites who were using them as de facto shields are scrambling to deal with both the good and bad results of this. On the good side, they have much more territory now. On the bad side, western cainites are now trickling in and trying to take over. The cainites of the east are really missing the kuejin, who were never all that numerous due to the excruciatingly slow method of their reproduction. The cainites of the east loved that these overrated, small in number, slow to reproduce, easy to avoid creatures inspired such terror from their western brethren. The kuejin were the boogeymen who protected the eastern cainites from western cainite invasion.<br /> <br /> Now that's over, and war is commencing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sadly this seems the most likely...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T23:09:47-07:00","id":1378192,"title":"","content":"Actually they probably would do an asspull like that at of nowhere to deal with an &quot;inconvenient&quot; plot piece they don't like. Disregarding that though the whole reason why they pulled oWoD out from the &quot;Abyss&quot; so to speak was for us to enjoy the splats again with the whole &quot;Time of Judgment/Gehenna&quot; thing they did out the way. The whole point of continuing on the lore was to ignore all aspects of Gehenna. Doing that to the Kuei-Jin to otherly wipe them out is nonsense. If you want Kuei-Jin to be within the VTM line and have a Time of Judgment-like to deal with them, Kindred are going to face their end too. This is why I honestly think having Kuei-Jin be considered really part of VTM is very waning tbh. Just like Mummy, they started as a spinoff within VTM but became their own splat in their own right. Using another splat to take down another for convenience is horrible (like how Mage through the Void Engineers ruined Wraith with Xerxes Jones) and asinine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-03-2020, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T00:50:39-07:00","id":1378202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378191#post1378191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sadly this seems the most likely...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that they twist the knife in a different direction, putting them all under a small number of clans a la the Heketa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T01:23:00-07:00","id":1378205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378185#post1378185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That may be something that they formed in Japanese (as shinta, which is listed right next to it) and back-read into some really mangled Wade-Giles Romanized Mandarin. Hazarding a guess, a simple \u795e\u4ed6, as Japanese sometimes uses \u795e for thunder. If that's an unsatisfying answer that doesn't work within the bounds of the languages in question... that's a depressing par for course, I'd say.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I can tell you \u795e in Japanese never has this meaning. Even in shi'n ta I still can't find answer<br /> <br /> *All oriental elements in KotE are, very ridiculous to us native speakers<br /> <br /> I still rememebr all. At first we even suspected we were reading ghost stories, just like <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Strange Tales of Liao Zhai (\u300a\u804a\u658b\u5fd7\u5f02\u300b). And we can't recongnize all names and tales except those in real history (Ru Shou, the first celestial blacksmith, Kingdom of Fu Yi... ). And some stereotypes are boring. Nevermind</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-03-2020, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T08:13:54-07:00","id":1378270,"title":"","content":"I would be deeply sad if they canned the Wan Kuei for the V5 line, but i could understand it. For my own part i've made them a global splat like the Mummies became, did some rejiggering of the setting to fit them in and explain why they are so rare in the West and so on. I would like some support from White Wolf for the splat, but at this point i have my own V20 setting and have it all the way i want. I hope they find a way to bring them back and make them a global splat as i did, but i want a lot of things and dont always get them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T12:06:49-07:00","id":1378315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378205#post1378205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I can tell you \u795e in Japanese never has this meaning. Even in shi'n ta I still can't find answer<br /> <br /> *All oriental elements in KotE are, very ridiculous to us native speakers<br /> <br /> I still rememebr all. At first we even suspected we were reading ghost stories, just like <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Strange Tales of Liao Zhai (\u300a\u804a\u658b\u5fd7\u5f02\u300b). And we can't recongnize all names and tales except those in real history (Ru Shou, the first celestial blacksmith, Kingdom of Fu Yi... ). And some stereotypes are boring. Nevermind</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Even if it doesn't make any sense to native speakers, if it shows up as an entry in a dictionary, it might still be something that the WW writers of the late 90s decided to go in on full bore. And, looking at wiktionary and jisho.org, there are entries for it as an archaic use of the character, so it's not out of the question that someone saw a loose connection in another source back in the day and decided to just go with it, lacking anyone to tell them that it was a bad idea (much like just dumping in the AD&amp;D version of Tou Mu as a character).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T12:54:57-07:00","id":1378320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1377979#post1377979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, as a native chinese I just want WW to revise, not retcon KotE. I hope they can simply ignore all stupid racism things, stereotypes and broken languages and all those out of date, repair the flawed system and make a more international, modern KotE. The general structure and theme are good and interesting</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I second that approach. As I mentioned in another thread on the subject, KotE was a line which incorporated almost everything the canon VtM lacked. I liked it very much and I hope we get a revision not a retcon.<br /> <br /> Rock113, may I ask you please, as a native chinese, what elements of KotE you liked the most? Dharmas, sects, societies, mechanics, disciplines (powers) or anything less specific? I always wondered what people native to the region and culture found interesting in it, in spite of all the shallow racism and stereotypes?<br /> What would you play the most in the game if (hopefully when) it finally makes it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T17:56:18-07:00","id":1378419,"title":"","content":"They should get native Asian writers (as appropriate for each country)<br /> <br /> Reading some of the KotE materials on the wiki leave me cringing. ( I'm new to the game, but I have been reading the wiki and some materials over the years.)<br /> <br /> Stereotyping of Asian cultures seems very common in western trpgs. Even now a days, I would come across scenarios/game modules set in a Asian or Asian inspired setting, but clearly written by someone whose understanding of Asian culture or themes came from watching movies and searching online.<br /> <br /> Case in point there was a scenario I ran set in an Asian inspired temple. The bad guy was supposed to be disguised as the head of the temple. The moment I spoke his name, one player was like why is he named for &quot;Big Hole&quot; in a Chinese dialect? And immediately deduce that he must be a bad guy. Likely the writer just google for a Chinese sounding name.<br /> (For the next run I changed the head of the temple name to something more appropriate for a temple head, in this case roughly &quot;Great Peace&quot; in Chinese.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26067,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","user":"Wingstorm","date":". 04-03-2020, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T17:59:34-07:00","id":1378422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378102#post1378102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it will be like you choose a Clan, then you choose a Dharma, kind of like Werewolf? Are you going to introduce new Clan Variants?<br /> <br /> It would be interesting because the Dharmas interact and form groups with each other, Forming Wu's if I recall their Coterie equivalent were. So its like a region that kept their Old Roads (The way vampires divided in the Dark Ages). Its interesting because if you make the different courts different sects its like a region with lots of potential rivals except people often stay in their own territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have an answer to this yet... That seems like a good dark ages model to use though. I really just want to open up Asia to telling vampire stories. Since my current game will focus on collecting the kue jin lore from inside the abandoned Las Vegas chantry, I guess I need to figure it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T18:34:09-07:00","id":1378436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wingstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378419#post1378419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They should get native Asian writers (as appropriate for each country)<br /> <br /> Reading some of the KotE materials on the wiki leave me cringing. ( I'm new to the game, but I have been reading the wiki and some materials over the years.)<br /> <br /> Stereotyping of Asian cultures seems very common in western trpgs. Even now a days, I would come across scenarios/game modules set in a Asian or Asian inspired setting, but clearly written by someone whose understanding of Asian culture or themes came from watching movies and searching online.<br /> <br /> Case in point there was a scenario I ran set in an Asian inspired temple. The bad guy was supposed to be disguised as the head of the temple. The moment I spoke his name, one player was like why is he named for &quot;Big Hole&quot; in a Chinese dialect? And immediately deduce that he must be a bad guy. Likely the writer just google for a Chinese sounding name.<br /> (For the next run I changed the head of the temple name to something more appropriate for a temple head, in this case roughly &quot;Great Peace&quot; in Chinese.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not always viable, especially not for each country because then if you get a book covering a region and you are budgeted for only a few writers you can't fit them in. And Malcom Shephard I don't think is Asian but he grew up in a buddhist family and was very qualified in my opinion to do his projects, like Dragons of the East. That said I believe the Mage book specifically made an attempt to get writers from different backgrounds to help write the different traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T01:53:18-07:00","id":1378487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378436#post1378436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is not always viable, especially not for each country because then if you get a book covering a region and you are budgeted for only a few writers you can't fit them in. And Malcom Shephard I don't think is Asian but he grew up in a buddhist family and was very qualified in my opinion to do his projects, like Dragons of the East. That said I believe the Mage book specifically made an attempt to get writers from different backgrounds to help write the different traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe they can have it looked over by a native speaker or get their input to help ensure it's culture appropriate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T08:14:02-07:00","id":1378548,"title":"","content":"Having lived in a god-forsaken part of China, and having a degree in buddhism and Chinese history, I really, really appreciate the Kindred of the East. They're extremely compelling beings with many features that makes them arguably more interesting than Cainites. For example, their beast had more personality, and they weren't immortal undead due to a random stranger's whims, but due to karmic debt, which made for very compelling stories. They also had that desperate distant hope of liberation through insight, which made their existence not entirely filled with doom and gloom. They also -felt- more properly undead than the Cainites, having the appropriate powers to actually interact with other undead (i.e ghost). I've made a long blog post in the past defending the merits of Kindred of the East's concept, it can be found <a href=\"http://trueartisangsty.blogspot.com/2017/08/why-kindred-of-east-is-better-than.html\" target=\"_blank\">here. </a><br /> <br /> I dearly hope the new writers of Vampire don't axe the Kindred of the East, for vampires in Asia shouldn't be forced into the judeo-christian mythological framework of Vampire - the Masquerade, but rather be allowed to exist within their own dharmic cosmology, the second of the two major cosmologies that have dominated in our world. That cosmology is extremely complex and shock-full of otherworldly realms, bizarre beings and fascinating concepts, yet sees way too little love in Western fantasy. Kindred of the East was terrific because of that, though yes, it could have been much better - and it will be, this time around! To make the vampires of Asia just ordinary Cainities with some token nudge to dharmic cosmology, while truly just forcing them into the monotheistic Vampire myth, would be to squander the immense potential of the dharmic concepts that made Kindred of the East so compelling in the first place.<br /> <br /> Asian cities in general are also soo perfect for World of Darkness' themes, being hyper-active, almost frenetic nexuses of intense human activity and street life, yet dirty, downtrodden and crumbling, with enormous contrasts between new and old, rich and poor, love and death. As long as Asia exists in a vacuum in V5, that potential is squandered, and with India in particular, where the abrahamitic and dharmic worlds meet, and which would therefore be such a great buffer zone for two kinds of vampires, the Western and the Eastern, that is a huge waste. But so would it be to just fill India with Cainites. India needs, and deserves, vampires that, as beings, exist in a state and world befitting the native worldview and all its awesome concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","user":"Natsymir","date":". 04-04-2020, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T18:43:16-07:00","id":1378648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378548#post1378548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> India needs, and deserves, vampires that, as beings, exist in a state and world befitting the native worldview and all its awesome concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone is arguing with this statement. But I suspect no one involved in WoD production feels qualified, or is thought by others to be qualified, to hit that very reasonable mark. WW people tried before, with the best intentions, and badly failed. The current people do not want to fall down the same hole. So it is being sidelined for the foreseeable future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T19:55:28-07:00","id":1378661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378648#post1378648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think anyone is arguing with this statement. But I suspect no one involved in WoD production feels qualified, or is thought by others to be qualified, to hit that very reasonable mark. WW people tried before, with the best intentions, and badly failed. The current people do not want to fall down the same hole. So it is being sidelined for the foreseeable future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah...you might be right. But I'm an experienced RPG writer in Sweden, maybe I should encourage them to employ me. *^_^*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","user":"Natsymir","date":". 04-04-2020, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T22:02:23-07:00","id":1378674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378548#post1378548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having lived in a god-forsaken part of China, and having a degree in buddhism and Chinese history, I really, really appreciate the Kindred of the East. They're extremely compelling beings with many features that makes them arguably more interesting than Cainites. For example, their beast had more personality, and they weren't immortal undead due to a random stranger's whims, but due to karmic debt, which made for very compelling stories. They also had that desperate distant hope of liberation through insight, which made their existence not entirely filled with doom and gloom. They also -felt- more properly undead than the Cainites, having the appropriate powers to actually interact with other undead (i.e ghost). I've made a long blog post in the past defending the merits of Kindred of the East's concept, it can be found <a href=\"http://trueartisangsty.blogspot.com/2017/08/why-kindred-of-east-is-better-than.html\" target=\"_blank\">here. </a><br /> <br /> I dearly hope the new writers of Vampire don't axe the Kindred of the East, for vampires in Asia shouldn't be forced into the judeo-christian mythological framework of Vampire - the Masquerade, but rather be allowed to exist within their own dharmic cosmology, the second of the two major cosmologies that have dominated in our world. That cosmology is extremely complex and shock-full of otherworldly realms, bizarre beings and fascinating concepts, yet sees way too little love in Western fantasy. Kindred of the East was terrific because of that, though yes, it could have been much better - and it will be, this time around! To make the vampires of Asia just ordinary Cainities with some token nudge to dharmic cosmology, while truly just forcing them into the monotheistic Vampire myth, would be to squander the immense potential of the dharmic concepts that made Kindred of the East so compelling in the first place.<br /> <br /> Asian cities in general are also soo perfect for World of Darkness' themes, being hyper-active, almost frenetic nexuses of intense human activity and street life, yet dirty, downtrodden and crumbling, with enormous contrasts between new and old, rich and poor, love and death. As long as Asia exists in a vacuum in V5, that potential is squandered, and with India in particular, where the abrahamitic and dharmic worlds meet, and which would therefore be such a great buffer zone for two kinds of vampires, the Western and the Eastern, that is a huge waste. But so would it be to just fill India with Cainites. India needs, and deserves, vampires that, as beings, exist in a state and world befitting the native worldview and all its awesome concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I see your point, I also see the point of the people who say that people in Asian countries mostly just like Western vampires better. There's a reason that Hellsing's Alucard and Seras Victoria are Western vampires despite being made in Japan. The hybrid of undead, sucubus, and Byronic creature that is the Western vampire just works better than the hybrid of undead and demon that is the Eastern vampire. It's just flat out something that we did better than them, as acknowledged by them.<br /> <br /> Consequently, the KOE are just flat out a marketing failure with the very people of the East itself. If a group of players in Tokyo want to run a vampire game, they're going to, for the most part, want to play as Western style undead/succubus/Byronic hybrids rather than undead/demon hybrids, because that's just flat out more entertaining for the majority of roleplayers regardless of their country of origin. That's not me saying that, that's players in those actual countries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T22:35:19-07:00","id":1378681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378674#post1378674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I see your point, I also see the point of the people who say that people in Asian countries mostly just like Western vampires better. There's a reason that Hellsing's Alucard and Seras Victoria are Western vampires despite being made in Japan. The hybrid of undead, sucubus, and Byronic creature that is the Western vampire just works better than the hybrid of undead and demon that is the Eastern vampire. It's just flat out something that we did better than them, as acknowledged by them.<br /> <br /> Consequently, the KOE are just flat out a marketing failure with the very people of the East itself. If a group of players in Tokyo want to run a vampire game, they're going to, for the most part, want to play as Western style undead/succubus/Byronic hybrids rather than undead/demon hybrids, because that's just flat out more entertaining for the majority of roleplayers regardless of their country of origin. That's not me saying that, that's players in those actual countries.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say they're better versus worse or anything like that. But Vampire the Masquerade is, and has always been, based on pop-culture vampires rather than actual mythology. In my experience, people play VtM because they want to play pop-culture vampires; that's the whole premise of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T00:45:57-07:00","id":1378693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378674#post1378674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I see your point, I also see the point of the people who say that people in Asian countries mostly just like Western vampires better. There's a reason that Hellsing's Alucard and Seras Victoria are Western vampires despite being made in Japan. The hybrid of undead, sucubus, and Byronic creature that is the Western vampire just works better than the hybrid of undead and demon that is the Eastern vampire. It's just flat out something that we did better than them, as acknowledged by them.<br /> <br /> Consequently, the KOE are just flat out a marketing failure with the very people of the East itself. If a group of players in Tokyo want to run a vampire game, they're going to, for the most part, want to play as Western style undead/succubus/Byronic hybrids rather than undead/demon hybrids, because that's just flat out more entertaining for the majority of roleplayers regardless of their country of origin. That's not me saying that, that's players in those actual countries.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh, I run KotE for a bunch of SE Asian ( Indo, Malay and Hakka Chinese) players who enjoy playing PCs based heavily in local folklore. So....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T00:48:44-07:00","id":1378694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378681#post1378681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't say they're better versus worse or anything like that. But Vampire the Masquerade is, and has always been, based on pop-culture vampires rather than actual mythology. In my experience, people play VtM because they want to play pop-culture vampires; that's the whole premise of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably why I prefer all the other WoD splats over Cainites, much easier to fit into various local folklores than the viral Kindred model.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T07:05:18-07:00","id":1378750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wingstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378487#post1378487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, maybe they can have it looked over by a native speaker or get their input to help ensure it's culture appropriate?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's much more appropriate. Then again a lot of things slip by edititing That Rites of the Blood product made several oversights and contradictions, some got last minute corrected when we pointed it out in the open development preview. Sometimes its hard for the editors, fans are obsessed and invested so we take note when a book seems to completely miss the point of other books. But some of the better writers do get advice for those who are of the cultures they are writing about. And that Rage Across the World Book had that confusing part where they though China was just a normal Garou territory so they had Silver Fangs ruling a Caern and they had Wendigo and Uktena operating a Caern in Africa.<br /> <br /> Its over all I guess they can work on being I guess Careful. The 90s were a different time though. I just don't want them to be so shy that they ignore the continent period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T07:54:31-07:00","id":1378757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Natsymir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378548#post1378548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having lived in a god-forsaken part of China, and having a degree in buddhism and Chinese history, I really, really appreciate the Kindred of the East. They're extremely compelling beings with many features that makes them arguably more interesting than Cainites. For example, their beast had more personality, and they weren't immortal undead due to a random stranger's whims, but due to karmic debt, which made for very compelling stories. They also had that desperate distant hope of liberation through insight, which made their existence not entirely filled with doom and gloom. They also -felt- more properly undead than the Cainites, having the appropriate powers to actually interact with other undead (i.e ghost). I've made a long blog post in the past defending the merits of Kindred of the East's concept, it can be found <a href=\"http://trueartisangsty.blogspot.com/2017/08/why-kindred-of-east-is-better-than.html\" target=\"_blank\">here. </a><br /> <br /> I dearly hope the new writers of Vampire don't axe the Kindred of the East, for vampires in Asia shouldn't be forced into the judeo-christian mythological framework of Vampire - the Masquerade, but rather be allowed to exist within their own dharmic cosmology, the second of the two major cosmologies that have dominated in our world. That cosmology is extremely complex and shock-full of otherworldly realms, bizarre beings and fascinating concepts, yet sees way too little love in Western fantasy. Kindred of the East was terrific because of that, though yes, it could have been much better - and it will be, this time around! To make the vampires of Asia just ordinary Cainities with some token nudge to dharmic cosmology, while truly just forcing them into the monotheistic Vampire myth, would be to squander the immense potential of the dharmic concepts that made Kindred of the East so compelling in the first place.<br /> <br /> Asian cities in general are also soo perfect for World of Darkness' themes, being hyper-active, almost frenetic nexuses of intense human activity and street life, yet dirty, downtrodden and crumbling, with enormous contrasts between new and old, rich and poor, love and death. As long as Asia exists in a vacuum in V5, that potential is squandered, and with India in particular, where the abrahamitic and dharmic worlds meet, and which would therefore be such a great buffer zone for two kinds of vampires, the Western and the Eastern, that is a huge waste. But so would it be to just fill India with Cainites. India needs, and deserves, vampires that, as beings, exist in a state and world befitting the native worldview and all its awesome concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent Article I pretty much agree with all your points, except I love Serpentis but I'm biased.<br /> <br /> If it makes a difference I'm Asian, I was born in Asia, I've lived with Asian Roommates from other Countries, and I've travel to China, and yeah I love Kindred of the East and its a great setting for the World of Darkness. Lil less Japanese Fetishism as Natsymir mentioned in his article. But they have a great set up for a game, and more hooks for making a compelling character. I agree with embraces being kind of cheap, I think my house rule will be Vampires at least need to spend a willpower point, won't make it a dot because Shovelheads are already canon. Hmm maybe V5 should have made Embraces require Exp or Willpower Dot burning.<br /> <br /> But I've long been an Advocate for the Idea that India is the Middle ground of the World of Darkness it is where the two paradigms of East and West meet and I wish we had a Rage Across India and something like New Delhi by Night, like we had the year of the Scarab and Year of the Lotus we should have Year of the Sharma or something to cover India.<br /> <br /> And my Favorite City book was Cairo by Night as well! But it was the first Vampire City book I read so I thought that effected my opinion but it sounds like no it was just great.<br /> <br /> But I would love to see my Mothercountry of the Philippines covered, I know someone has compiled a Storytellers Vault project for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T14:42:47-07:00","id":1378845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378757#post1378757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I would love to see my Mothercountry of the Philippines covered, I know someone has compiled a Storytellers Vault project for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Manila series ( 3 books) is actually REALLY good and I've used it a few times in my games when my lot have headed north out of Kalimantan. I definetely recommend 