ue":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T03:01:09-07:00","id":1379196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1379065#post1379065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A brief introduction to Philippines by Night (in spanish).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://webvampiro.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/Filipinas-Nocturno.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://webvampiro.com/wp-content/up...s-Nocturno.pdf</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh wow that's fantastic. Magus I see you every now and then post things like this that are completely off my radar. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T04:58:55-07:00","id":1379230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1378320#post1378320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rock113, may I ask you please, as a native chinese, what elements of KotE you liked the most? Dharmas, sects, societies, mechanics, disciplines (powers) or anything less specific? I always wondered what people native to the region and culture found interesting in it, in spite of all the shallow racism and stereotypes?<br /> What would you play the most in the game if (hopefully when) it finally makes it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I find that I like the simple concepts except cultural elements involved in, power increased by the Enlightment, treat Ages as Wheel, the theme of redemption, the complex philosophy, the fallen demigod heroes, the two-side essence (Yin and Yang). We will reset all cultural things if playing it.<br /> <br /> I will play the progress of enlightment and battle the most.<br /> <br /> * To be honest the original reason why I read this line is &quot;hunt for novelty&quot;, how do the foreigners view us? I think it's, okay<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T15:30:54-07:00","id":1379334,"title":"","content":"Retcon all the published materials about the Kuei-Jin and the previous mentions of them as misinformed propaganda. Remake them completely and base them around actual specific Asian vampire archetypes. <br /> That\u2019s what I hope happens, at least. And I really like them not being descendants of Caine. It feels gross and weird to have all of Asia be populated by creatures that originate from mythology of western religion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25975-queenherla","name":"QueenHerla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25975_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T15:33:30-07:00","id":1379336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QueenHerla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1379334#post1379334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Retcon all the published materials about the Kuei-Jin and the previous mentions of them as misinformed propaganda. Remake them completely and base them around actual specific Asian vampire archetypes.<br /> That\u2019s what I hope happens, at least. And I really like them not being descendants of Caine. It feels gross and weird to have all of Asia be populated by creatures that originate from mythology of western religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>... that's already what they were, they used things like the Penangallan, Aswang and Menannangal when they designed them. They incorporated things from an Eastern Paradigm with the 1000 Hells and the weight of Karma damning you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T15:35:21-07:00","id":1379339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1379336#post1379336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... that's already what they were, they used things like the Penangallan, Aswang and Menannangal when they designed them. They incorporated things from an Eastern Paradigm with the 1000 Hells and the weight of Karma damning you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the main Dharmas, the most meaningful factions for the PCs, didn\u2019t really correspond to vampiric archetypes. Though I do like the KJ\u2019s religion-based society.<br /> <br /> Asia is the largest continent and the most populous and the Kuei-Jim conflated a lot of different cultures to something improbably homogenous. A vampire culture in Asia should be much more fractured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25975-queenherla","name":"QueenHerla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25975_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T15:38:33-07:00","id":1379340,"title":"","content":"There is a germ of a great idea in the Kuei-jin, honestly. But they absolutely need to hire Asian writers to do any more supplements about Asia in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25975-queenherla","name":"QueenHerla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25975_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T16:33:11-07:00","id":1379351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QueenHerla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1379339#post1379339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but the main Dharmas, the most meaningful factions for the PCs, didn\u2019t really correspond to vampiric archetypes. Though I do like the KJ\u2019s religion-based society.<br /> <br /> Asia is the largest continent and the most populous and the Kuei-Jim conflated a lot of different cultures to something improbably homogenous. A vampire culture in Asia should be much more fractured.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">There is a germ of a great idea in the Kuei-jin, honestly. But they absolutely need to hire Asian writers to do any more supplements about Asia in the future. </span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>But that's the thing with the X-Y Axis, both don't correspond with myth, usually one like the X Axis will correspond to folklore and the Y will be a fabrication of the Unique system of the Setting. Like Werewolves have tribes influenced by cultures but the Auspices are phases of the moon, Garou are made for the setting they aren't directly from a specific werewolf myth and are more Animistic beings.<br /> <br /> So with Wan Gui they have the Dharma which I feel were handled Brilliantly, but they don't really have a Y Axis so you have Courts as kind of like the Sects of the Kin-jin. You sound like you want an X axis that is the type of Vampire you are that represents something you didn't choose and a Y Axis that would be I guess the Dharmas. They didn't do that but that is because they didn't embrace the X-Y Axis with a Z optional Axis till they did NWOD.<br /> <br /> But as it stands it works the way you describe because courts are based more around regional Myths, and Farther Away from the strong Courts you get the old Heretical Dharmas which fit well with regional myths. If we did it your way you would have more obvious dissonance with the fact that you would have things that Follow the Aswang Myth for instance in Beijing as they would make up one of I don't 5 or 7 main splats. But currently its the best of both worlds because we have the Courts combined with specialized Disciplines and the Heretical Dharmas. We can have Flesh Shintai wielders in Beijing but they won't be obvious and in your face like if you go to Indonesia.<br /> <br /> Honestly it just sounds like if they made the Courts more prominent a faction that you could join out of Region it would fit your criteria. Because as things goes the Wan Gui fit both Western and Eastern various Vampire Myths better then Cainites who are strongly influenced more by Anne Rice in my opinion.<br /> <br /> I do agree it would be helpful to have those from Asian cultures as writer, but its something that will be needing work to cultivate because Table Top RPGs are Niche hobbies, and my friends don't know of Whitewolf games unless I mention it. I have a friend who had to stop his DnD game in China because of quarantine and baby birth. This section of the Hobby is niche. Its more important to me that you have a writer who knows the world and can do research rather then just hire someone only because they fit the criteria of being ambiguously Asian. Someone who does know about these games will have a greater likelihood of being American (well western born) Born because these games don't have a robust spread of translations. And even if they were Asian they would only have a perspective of being native from area, so being from Singapore will only give them mild cultural bleed over from say Korea. What you need is writers, any of them, that have friends or professionals to help them research or consult.<br /> <br /> It really sounds unnecessary to wipe the slate clean because you want them literally have splats based on specific vampire myths when the Wan Gui already cover most of the Myths by the fact that they are Unquiet dead.<br /> <br /> It really makes sense the root of Mainstream Wan Gui culture would stem from India and China, with places like Korea and Japan having diverging sub cultures, and having rural and isolated portions of those countries as well as others like the Philippines and Malaysia having strongly diverged groups with less influence from the mainstream Wan Gui (so animism and local variations of Yomi and the Yama Kings colour it, like having Rangda is different then Mikaboshi as your big bad).<br /> <br /> But Ultimate there needs to be a layer of fiction to separate the books from just being point for point copy and paste because humanity doesn't know their whole history and the Myths and Folklore are Human adaptions to looking at these beings. As Malcom Shepard said they couldn't just make Mage literally the same as the Buddhist legends because that is kind of disrespectful you have to have a secret history of the world that is different that if you are familiar with the real culture and legends you can go ohh I see so humanity thinks this because these beings are actually like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T17:18:54-07:00","id":1379356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QueenHerla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1379339#post1379339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but the main Dharmas, the most meaningful factions for the PCs, didn\u2019t really correspond to vampiric archetypes. Though I do like the KJ\u2019s religion-based society.<br /> <br /> Asia is the largest continent and the most populous and the Kuei-Jim conflated a lot of different cultures to something improbably homogenous. A vampire culture in Asia should be much more fractured.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps not to the current asian vampiric archetype. Western vampiric archetypes were created around current religious myths (vampires descend from Cain and the judaism appeared during canaaite times around 1000 BC, though the claim to be older) and those weren't around during the origins of cainites.. Asian kueijin are created from the chinese myths of jiangxie and much of its superstitions, same happen here. The current myths of kueijin weren't around the time of Xue, Zao-lat and Ki Chuan and their origins yet they are adapted towards their most current culture of the area. Plus back in the day, internet wasn't as big as it is now, so I'd say the writers did a really fine job with Kindred of the East.<br /> <br /> Diversity between cultures can be found in the division between Qincunx (china), Uji (japan) and the Golden Courts (southeast asia). I understand your point that asian vampires perhaps should be completely different in essence (cainite/kueijin/etc) between such cultures, but remember that the same thing happen with cainites and they aren't (many cultures like precolumbian, european, african, scandinavian and all are clans from a single progenitor). Their division is in the social organization among them, not in their vampiric physiology.<br /> <br /> India being the nexus between cainites (ravnos) and kueijin (heretic dharmas and infinite thunders court) is a great setting to work with.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 04-07-2020, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T14:16:15-07:00","id":1379521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh wow that's fantastic. Magus I see you every now and then post things like this that are completely off my radar. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Perhaps I'll extend it with the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:08:27-07:00","id":1379843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1379230#post1379230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I find that I like the simple concepts except cultural elements involved in, power increased by the Enlightment, treat Ages as Wheel, the theme of redemption, the complex philosophy, the fallen demigod heroes, the two-side essence (Yin and Yang). We will reset all cultural things if playing it.<br /> <br /> I will play the progress of enlightment and battle the most.<br /> <br /> * To be honest the original reason why I read this line is &quot;hunt for novelty&quot;, how do the foreigners view us? I think it's, okay<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you. Glad to know we loved the same about the game - basic concepts which, despite all of the cheap racism, felt to me like a refreshment after the constant drama and moral flagellation 'Crime and Punishment'-style we have in VtM. The sheer ambiguity - life and death are one vs constant fear of one or the other - and the concept of Karma and the cyclic nature of time instead of a linear in VtM honestly sold it for me instantly. I still recall my almost childish fascination with the corebook when I just started reading. I felt like, 'WAIT YOU COULD DO IT ALL ALONG!'. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T20:24:55-07:00","id":1380010,"title":"","content":"Back to the subject at hand...<br /> <br /> I expect MP and OP to ignore the issue of the Asian vampire society. But that could leave it open for fan productions. What would you say to that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T10:56:56-07:00","id":1380417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1377937-so-what-is-vampire-going-to-do-with-asia?p=1380010#post1380010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to the subject at hand...<br /> <br /> I expect MP and OP to ignore the issue of the Asian vampire society. But that could leave it open for fan productions. What would you say to that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that's a question rather to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24560_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24560\" data-vbnamecard=\"24560\">Rock113</a> . I'm a fan of KotE line, that's true, I am not quite sure I have knowledge of culture, understanding of the spiritual concepts or proficiency in language(s) necessary to start writing on it. As many here stated, it feels better to either fully handle the writing on Asian supernatural to the people native to the region and it's cultures or do heavy referencing.<br /> <br /> I would certainly try to outline my take on the revision of the world of Asian vampires and 2004-2020 changes though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:12:55-07:00","id":1380424,"title":"","content":"No problem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}